WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.752
Start with the packaged water X Y Z file. In Molecular data, check for three

00:00:05.752 --> 00:00:10.354
atoms and two display bonds. In Selections and measurements, select the first

00:00:10.354 --> 00:00:15.339
two atoms and use Geometry measurements to add an oxygen to hydrogen distance.

00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:20.931
Select hydrogen, oxygen, hydrogen in that order and add an angle. Oxygen is

00:00:20.931 --> 00:00:26.071
the vertex. The distance is about zero point nine five seven angstroms. The

00:00:26.071 --> 00:00:31.210
angle is about one hundred four point four six degrees. Export the measurement

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.373
table and a figure to document the result.

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:40.104
Open the one A O N structure and switch to protein cartoon. Select chain

00:00:40.104 --> 00:00:44.245
coloring to distinguish deposited copies. Switch to entity coloring to group

00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:49.516
copies that share an entity. Use the chain controls to isolate and frame a

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:54.033
copy, or the component controls to show ligands as ball and stick.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:00.075
Open ligands and neighborhoods to find a specific copy. Here A D P chain A

00:01:00.075 --> 00:01:04.535
residue one is the deposited author identity. Start each four angstrom search

00:01:04.535 --> 00:01:09.367
from that one ligand. The second search includes full residues, so it shows

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.225
more of the local context.

00:01:11.708 --> 00:01:16.750
Back in water, open Molecular surfaces. Build an excluded surface from all

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:22.633
three atoms. Use Bondi Mantina radii, a one point four angstrom probe, and a

00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:26.835
quarter angstrom grid. Compare the settings before generating the accessible

00:01:26.835 --> 00:01:31.036
surface. Save both so you can switch views without recalculating.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.208
Finish with an image that shows the result, a measurement table with units,

00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:42.003
and a native file for future editing. This one A O N figure records the local

00:01:42.003 --> 00:01:46.349
contact as a geometric distance. Keep its source identifiers and view settings

00:01:46.349 --> 00:01:47.436
with the figure.
